#: patterns/faq.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Frequently asked questions in an accordion beside a short section heading."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:10
msgid "How long does a project usually take?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:11
msgid "A full product engagement runs six weeks end to end. An identity is three to four. A second opinion is one week. If your deadline is tighter than that, tell me early and I will say honestly whether it fits."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:15
msgid "Is the price fixed?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:16
msgid "Yes, wherever the scope is defined. One number, one payment schedule and a written list of what sits inside it. Anything outside becomes a conversation before work starts, never a surprise line on an invoice."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:20
msgid "Can you work alongside our engineers?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:21
msgid "That is the normal arrangement. I join your stand-ups, write specs in whatever format your team already uses, and stay reachable for a month after handover so questions get answered rather than guessed at."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:25
msgid "What lands in my hands at the end?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:26
msgid "Source files, a component library with every state documented, a token sheet, exported assets and a written spec covering behaviour and edge cases. Build engagements also include block patterns and a configured theme.json."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:30
msgid "Do you take small pieces of work?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:31
msgid "Sometimes. A single landing page, a pricing rewrite or a one-week review all fit comfortably. Anything larger tends to work better as a short sprint than as hours scattered across a quarter."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:35
msgid "Who owns the work at the end?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:36
msgid "You do, completely, once the final payment clears. Files transfer into your accounts rather than living in mine. I only ask permission to show the work publicly, and I will keep it private if you would rather."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:45
#: patterns/header.php:39
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:49
msgid "Asked before nearly every project."
msgstr ""

